# Raw Kaggle export is ~493MB -- too large to commit, and not ours to redistribute.
# README explains how to fetch it; data/processed/spotify_threads.jsonl ships the
# small derived subsample instead (that one file IS committed).
dataset/

# Retrieval index: committed despite being regenerable (`python -m
# src.retrieve`, ~45s locally) because app.py is deployed on Streamlit
# Community Cloud, which clones a fresh checkout with no build step -- an
# uncommitted index would mean every deploy rebuilds it live (~4,000
# embedding calls against the free NIM tier) before the app can serve a
# single visitor. Not worth the fragility for a 32MB binary.

# Trained baseline classifier cache -- regenerates from golden_set.csv.
results/simple_baseline_classifier.pkl